From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:34:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Report broken documents where and as Windows does.

tools/msxmlmoreprobe in the wine-altars repository loaded fourteen broken
documents into MSXML 3.0 and 6.0 on Windows 11 and printed what
parseError said about each.  Three of them Wine took as well-formed:

- A reference to an undeclared entity is XML_ENTITY_UNDEFINED
  (0xc00ce002) when there is no DTD, or one whose declarations were all
  read: no external subset and no parameter entity references, or a
  standalone document (the "Entity Declared" well-formedness
  constraint).  Otherwise it stays a skipped entity.
- A character text may not hold, a control character other than tab,
  line feed and carriage return, or U+FFFE or U+FFFF, is
  XML_E_BADCHARDATA (0xc00ce508).
- What follows the root element: another element is
  XML_E_MULTIPLEROOTS (0xc00ce555), anything else other than spaces,
  comments and processing instructions XML_E_INVALIDATROOTLEVEL.

The input ending inside a start tag is XML_E_UNCLOSEDSTARTTAG
(0xc00ce55e) at its name, and inside an element an error with no
position.  Most errors are at the character the parser reached; a
duplicate attribute at the end of its start tag; a bad version in the
declaration at its value.  parseError gives the line's text as srcText
and the error's offset in the text as filepos, for loadXML, load and
data from a URL, and an empty string loads with XML_E_MISSINGROOT.

What the probe printed is now Windows' for every document but the
message texts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/msxml3/domdoc.c b/dlls/msxml3/domdoc.c
